```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let raw = crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("subscriptions").unwrap_or_default();
        let urls: Vec<String> = raw
            .lines()
            .map(|l| l.trim())
            .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
            .map(|l| l.to_string())
            .collect();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

Two assumptions to check: the store holds the URLs as newline-separated text under the key `subscriptions`, and a missing key gives an empty list rather than an invented URL. If `present(urls)` is meant to require a non-empty list, an empty store would violate it. I read it as "the field is populated from the store", since the node has no authority to fabricate subscriptions.

